372	// SVG sanitising
373	//
374	// AN UPLOADED SVG IS UNTRUSTED CODE, NOT A PICTURE. It gets inlined into a page
375	// served from *.kodely.site under a CSP that permits 'unsafe-inline' script, so
376	// a single surviving `onload=` is stored XSS on the customer's own domain.
377	//
378	// The design here is allowlist-only and, critically, RE-SERIALISING: nothing
379	// from the input reaches the output as bytes. Element names come from a fixed
380	// table, attribute names come from a fixed table, and every value is validated
381	// against a per-attribute pattern and then re-escaped by our own writer. A
382	// parser differential between this scanner and a browser can therefore produce
383	// a mangled logo, but it cannot produce an attribute or an element that is not
384	// on these lists.
385	//
386	// Two distinct responses, on purpose:
387	//   REJECT — anything whose presence means the file is an attack or a trap
388	//            (script, event handlers, foreignObject, entity subsets, CDATA,
389	//            non-local hrefs). Silently stripping these would hide an attack;
390	//            a customer uploading a real logo never trips them.
391	//   STRIP  — anything merely unknown (editor metadata, sodipodi/inkscape
392	//            namespaces, filters, animation). Reported back so the UI can say
393	//            what was dropped.
394	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
